{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lesley Gore feels especially relevant because AM Gold: The Mid-'60s and my recent nostalgic collections make me want more familiar 1960s pop.",
    "Eagles and Fleetwood Mac feel like natural next choices because their melodic rock and harmonies connect with my interest in Simon & Garfunkel, The Cars, and classic rock collections. Elvis also fits my interest in older hit singles."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Earth Wind & Fire and Simply Red offer hit collections, but their funk and smooth pop sounds are less appealing right now than the folk and classic rock I have been revisiting.",
    "Greatest Hits and Very Best Of leave me unsure whose music I would hear, so I cannot judge whether they match my interests. The Christmas collection feels relevant, but I would need to know the performers before choosing it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations lean too heavily on greatest-hits collections; liking that format does not mean I want every artist represented in it.",
    "Older music seems to be treated as broadly interchangeable, although the sound and performers matter more to me than simply belonging to an earlier era."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in folk, melodic classic rock, and mid-1960s pop matters more right now than my occasional interest in other pop styles.",
    "My latest Christmas album makes seasonal music worth considering, but it does not outweigh my preference for recognizable performers and music that fits my current listening interests."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in nostalgic collections but sometimes extended it beyond the sounds and performers I currently want."
}"}
